// `Character.toLowerCase`/`toUpperCase` on v2 — the locale-independent Unicode case fold that
// `MarkdownLexer.foldCase` needs and that no UniML-side table can reasonably replace.
// Closed v2-side 2026-08-16 (`v2/src/Runtime.scala`, `characterFold`); the gap map
// (`specs/uniml-portable-gapmap.md`) lists this as one of the two admissible fixes.
//
// THIS PROBE CHECKS ITS OWN ANSWER, and that is not ceremony. The failure mode of this gap is not a
// crash: an unbound capitalized receiver lowers to an EFFECT OPERATION, so the program prints
// `Op("Character.toLowerCase", Α, <closure>)` and exits 0. `run.sh` classifies by grepping for
// `unbound global|Exception|IndexOutOfBounds`, so a wrong VALUE with a clean exit reads as PASS.
// Comparing the result and throwing is what makes the probe able to fail at all.
def need(got: Char, want: Char, what: String): Unit =
  if got != want then throw new RuntimeException("gap-char: " + what)

// Greek: the case that ASCII folding gets wrong, and the reason the fold is here at all.
need(Character.toLowerCase('Α'), 'α', "Greek capital alpha did not fold")
need(Character.toUpperCase('α'), 'Α', "Greek small alpha did not raise")
// ASCII still answers, so the fix cannot be "only the exotic path works".
need(Character.toLowerCase('A'), 'a', "ASCII A did not fold")
// An already-folded char is returned unchanged rather than mangled.
need(Character.toLowerCase('q'), 'q', "lowercase q did not stay put")

println("gap-char: OK")
